===Etymology 2===
Attested in the pita or flatbread sense since 1107.<br>

{{unc|gkm}}. Likely related to {{cog|nap|pizza}}, also of {{unk|gkm|nocap=1}} origin. 

* Suggested to be derived from {{der|grc|xil|-}}, whence {{bor|grc|sq|pite||gruel}} and {{m|sq|pitë||cake, bread, pastry}}, further suggested to be related to {{m|sq|petë|t=layer}}. Compare also {{cog|ro|pată|t=blotch, stain, macula}} and possibly {{cog|grc|πιττάκιον|t=patch; tablet; ticket}} — a word only attested from the 5<sup>th</sup> century, first in the works for the comedian [[w:sh:Dinoloh|Deinolochus]], and perhaps derived from the {{der|grc|ine-pro|-}} root from which one or more of the Albanian words is inherited. 
* Alternatively, the {{der|gkm|qfa-sub}} could also be Jewish {{der|grc|arc|פִיתָּא|tr=pītā|t=piece of bread}}, from {{der|grc|sem-pro|-}} root related to crumbs and breaking into tranches, akin to {{cog|he|פַּת|tr=paṯ|t=bread}} and the {{cog|ar|-}} forms in the root {{ar-root|ف ت ت|nocat=1}}, also {{cog|tig|-}} / {{cog|ti|-}} / {{cog|am|-}} / {{cog|gez|ፈተተ|t=to break off, to portion, to crumb}}.

