* with a stressed falling diphthong, the semivowel is dropped, e.g. {{m|pt|r'''e'''al}} (from {{m|pt|r'''ei'''}}) and {{m|pt|id'''e'''al}} (from {{m|pt|id'''ei'''a}}); or
* with an unstressed ''o'' not following an ''i'' (mostly derived from Latin fourth declension), the form {{m|pt|-ual}} may be used instead, e.g. {{m|pt|text'''ual'''}} (from {{m|pt|text'''o'''}}) but {{m|pt|pred'''ial'''}} (from {{m|pt|préd'''io'''}}) instead of *''prediual''.
The ending may appear as {{m|pt|-ial}} or {{m|pt|-eal}} (e.g. {{m|pt|racial}}, from {{m|pt|raça}}, and {{m|pt|floreal}}, from {{m|pt|flor}}).

