#: {{suffixusex|la|līber|t1=free, independent, unrestricted; open, unbiased|-ālis|līberālis|t3=advocating and promoting personal freedom; bountiful, generous}}
#: {{suffixusex|la|socius|t1=associating, sharing, partaking|-ālis|sociālis|t3=companionable; allied, confederate}}

====Usage notes====
The suffix ''-ālis'' is added (usually, but not exclusively) to a [[noun]] or [[numeral]] to form an [[adjective]] of relationship to that noun. When suffixed to an existing adjective, the effect is and to [[intensify]] the adjectival [[meaning]], and often to [[narrow]] the [[semantic field]]. If the root word ends in {{m|la|-l}} or {{m|la|-lis}}, {{m|la|-āris}} is generally used instead. Sometimes both forms are found; e.g., {{m|la|līneālis}} and {{m|la|līneāris}}.

