===Etymology===
{{etymon|grc|id=call|:der|ine-pro:*kelh₁-}}
From {{der|grc|ine-pro||*kl̥h₁-}}, zero-grade of {{m|ine-pro|*kelh₁-|t=to call}}. According to Beekes, the term perhaps emerged as a {{back-formation|nocap=1|grc|-}} the aorist {{m|grc|ἐκάλεσα}}.<ref>{{R:grc:Beekes|head=καλέω|pages=623}}</ref> Alternatively, the LIV suggests an earlier zero-grade ''éye''-present {{m|ine-pro||*kl̥h₁-éye-ti}}.<ref>{{R:ine:LIV|*kleh₁-|pages=361-362}}</ref>

Cognates include {{cog|ang|hlōwan}} and {{cog|en|low|pos=verb}} (but the similarity to {{m|en|call}} is coincidental); {{cog|la|calō}}, {{m|la|clāmō}}, {{m|la|clārus}}, {{m|la|classis}}, and {{m|la|concilium}}; {{cog|sga|cailech}}; {{cog|xcl|աքաղաղ}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{grc-IPA|κᾰλέω}}

===Verb===
{{grc-verb|head=κᾰλέω}}

# to [[call]], [[summon]]
#: {{uxi|grc|'''Κάλει''' με/'''Κάλεσόν''' με.|Call me.}}
## to [[invite]]
##* {{Q|grc|NT|John|2|2}}
## to [[invoke]]
##* {{Q|grc|Herodotus|Histories|1|44|2}}
## {{lb|grc|legal}} to [[summon]], [[sue]]
##* {{Q|grc|Demosthenes|19|211}}
## to [[demand]], [[require]]
# to call by name
## {{lb|grc|passive}} to be called, one's name is
##* {{Q|grc|Herodotus|Histories|7|89|2|quote=τῆς δὲ Συρίης τοῦτο τὸ χωρίον καὶ τὸ μέχρι Αἰγύπτου πᾶν Παλαιστίνη '''καλέεται'''.|trans=This part of Syria as far as Egypt is all called Palestine.}}

====Usage notes====
* The Doric present forms {{m|grc|καλέομες}} and {{m|grc|καλέοισι}} are attested.
