===Verb===
{{en-verb|+,++}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause ([[ray]]s of [[light]], etc) to converge at a single point.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1961|month=February|title=Talking of Trains: Collision at Newcastle|journal=Trains Illustrated|pages=75–76|text=The difficulties of '''focussing''' colour-light signals on curved tracks to ensure maximum sighting distance were underlined in the recent official report [...] on a low-speed collision at Newcastle Central on July 25, 1960, between an unfitted freight and a diesel-hauled passenger train.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|optics}} To [[adjust]] (a [[lens]], an optical instrument) in order to position an image with respect to the [[focal plane]].
#: {{ux|en|You'll need to '''focus''' the microscope carefully in order to capture the full detail of this surface.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|optics|of a lens, optical instrument, etc.}} To [[adjust]] itself or be adjusted such that light from a scene converges appropriately to create a clear image.
#: {{ux|en|I can't get the lens to '''focus'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The camera '''focuses''' automatically on the subject's eyes.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To direct attention, effort, or energy to a particular audience or task.
#: {{ux|en|The president '''focused''' her remarks on the newcomers.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[concentrate]] one’s [[attention]].
#: {{ux|en|If you're going to beat your competitors, you need to '''focus'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|followed by '''on''' or '''upon'''}} To [[concentrate]] one's attention on something; to have as one's central point of interest, concern, etc.
#: {{ux|en|I have to '''focus''' on my work.}}
# {{lb|en|computing|GUI|transitive}} To transfer the [[input]] focus to (a visual element), so that it receives subsequent input.
#: {{ux|en|The text box won't receive the user's keystrokes unless you explicitly '''focus''' it.}}
