===Etymology===
* The origin is {{unc|la|nocap=1}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|pages=228-9|head=focus}}</ref> Usually connected with {{cog|xcl|բոց}}.
* Some connect this along with {{m|la|faciēs}}, {{m|la|facētus}}, {{m|la|fax}} to {{der|la|ine-pro|*bʰeh₂-|t=to shine}}; if so, cognate at the root level with {{cog|sa|भाति॑}}, {{cog|grc|φαίνω|t=to shine}}, etc.
* Matasović, and Hamp before him, opt to derive from {{der|la|ine-pro|*dʰegʷʰ-|t=to burn}}; Matasović believes that the {{m|la||-c-}} would have spread from the nominative of a root noun {{m|ine-pro||*dʰṓkʷʰ-s}} (< {{m|ine-pro||*dʰṓgʷʰ-s}}).<ref>{{cite-journal|last=Matasović|first=Ranko|title=The etymology of Latin {{m|la||focus}} and the devoicing of final stops before {{lang|ine-pro|*s}} in Proto-Indo-European|journal=Historische Sprachforschung|trans-journal=Historical Linguistics|publisher=Vandenhoeck & Ruprecht|volume=123|year=2010|issn=0935-3518|jstor=41219150|pages=212–216|url=http://www.jstor.org/stable/41219150}}</ref>

